Root Cause:
in the past we thought it is related to platform / bios. wake up interrupts takes time. after taking to the platform they thought it will be fixed in B step of TGL. this one here is AML and seems like sleep from the OS takes time (max time can be up to 16 ms). example: it means that sleep of 1us can take up to 16 ms.
Changed mechanism of osal wait that  in case of small amounts of sleep and in passive mode, the driver will busy wait.
comment from delivery:
    // if the wait is < 50 micro, we want to use osalUtilStallExecution instead of sleep because sleep is bound by system ticks and can be longer (up to 16ms)
    // than the original wait. osalUtilStallExecution time is more accurate
